            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a fruit seller, then the Urdu for a greengrocer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: انجن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انجن — injan — \"an engine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ریل گاڑی کا انجن کالا اور بڑا ہے۔ rel gāṛī kā injan kālā aur baṛā hai. The train's engine is big and black."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "انجن (injan) is borrowed from English engine; at a station it means the locomotive at the front of the train."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
