          "title": "You'll want to know: بجنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بجنا — bajnā — \"to sound; to ring\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اسٹیشن پر سیٹی بجی اور گاڑی چلی۔ isṭeshan par sīṭī bajī aur gāṛī chalī. The whistle sounded at the station and the train moved off."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): وہ سیٹی بجی, voh sīṭī bajī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بجنا (bajnā) is inherited: CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin bājnā, \"to sound\", under Sanskrit vādyate, \"is made to sound\" (CDIAL 11513). بجانا, \"to play an instrument\", is the form for making a thing sound, and بجے, \"o'clock\", is the hour that has struck."
            }
          ]
        },
